ourth quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n\n- $\\frac{3}{2}-\\text{i}$\n- $-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}$\n- $\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-79458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The complex number $\\frac{3}{2}-\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=-1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(\\frac{3}{2},-1)$, which lies in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2})$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and the imaginary part $y=\\frac{3}{2}.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$, which lies in the first quadrant.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/d7390ddcc8d338d2fd46bc12b0a4c65f8e6bf6e8c4f6c9fa802e2acea159416b.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-79458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b865ba79fbf8169508af077e38f520d8db966debb01dd90baeaf19c28d2d60d9"} {"question" "q-79458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-79458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-79458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following numbers lie in the second quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n\n- $-2+\\text{i}$\n- $-3-2\\text{i}$\n- $-3+2\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The complex number $-2+\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,1)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,-2)$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3+2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,2)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/d683b808bee4b7893952adbaf87940066f9ff7d61c99ce7cc7e05fc9a4fbe02f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b865ba79fbf8169508af077e38f520d8db966debb01dd90baeaf19c28d2d60d9"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "q-69899" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/state.json" "file_sha256" "e89302b6817cdd4fb162eab4472ed27252c0b6d7e0776ec2db54ef56d227fd46"} {"question" "e-5034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What complex number is represented in the Argand diagram below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/79285ea5c9dc4b535b972f40fb16c9deaf57d895b2081eb789d74663525e12d2.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/example-5034.json" "file_sha256" "c2cce5381a0539cd9d7e9c476e7307378186b9cfa22f55dfc2e2143fe9974dc2"} {"question" "e-5034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coordinates of the point are $(-2,3)$.\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=-2,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number depicted is $z=-2+3\\textrm{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/example-5034.json" "file_sha256" "c2cce5381a0539cd9d7e9c476e7307378186b9cfa22f55dfc2e2143fe9974dc2"} {"question" "e-5035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What complex number is represented in the Argand diagram below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/assets/7bcf26c8df340bc61e1863043ba2126dea07661c2e288fa5321ddd5ae9e67b46.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035975/example-5035.json" "file_sha256" "e6206607dfc813d23e727e0c76454192dd8cd6fcae1803272b33337cd07b16c0"} {"question" "e-5035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coordinates of the point are $(-4,0).$\n\n- The real part of this complex number is $x=-4,$ and\n\n- the imaginary part is $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the number depicted is $z=-4+0\\textrm{i},$ which can be simplified to $z= -4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacade